{'symbol': 'USB', 'date': '2019-10-16 09:30:00', 'title': 'U.S. Bancorp Reports Qtrly Earnings Per Share Of $1.15', 'text': 'QTRLY TOTAL NET REVENUE $5.92 BILLION VERSUS $5.70 BILLION.REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.15.QTRLY RETURN ON AVERAGE COMMON EQUITY 15.3% VERSUS 15.5% REPORTED LAST YEAR.TOTAL NET CHARGE-OFFS IN Q3 WERE $352 MILLION VERSUS $350 MILLION IN Q2.ALLOWANCE FOR CREDIT LOSSES WAS $4,481 MILLION AT SEPT. 30, 2019 VERSUS $4,466 MILLION AT JUNE 30, 2019.NET INTEREST INCOME ON TAXABLE-EQUIVALENT BASIS IN Q3 $3.31 BILLION VERSUS $3.28 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.11, REVENUE VIEW $5.82 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
{'symbol': 'USB', 'date': '2019-10-16 22:30:00', 'title': 'U.S. Bancorp Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'U.S. Bancorp announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced net interest income was USD 3,281 million compared to USD 3,251 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,908 million compared to USD 1,815 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.16 compared to USD 1.06 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.15 compared to USD 1.06 a year ago. For the nine months, net interest income was USD 9,845 million compared to USD 9,616 million a year ago. Net income was USD 5,428 million compared to USD 5,240 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.26 compared to USD 3.05 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 3.25 compared to USD 3.04 a year ago.'}
{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2019-10-16 14:30:00', 'title': "United Airlines has ability to keep costs flat by 'constantly getting more efficient'", 'text': "UNITED AIRLINES SAYS NO NEED TO RETIRE WIDEBODIES OVER NEXT FIVE YEARS -CONF CALL.UNITED AIRLINES SAYS IT HAS INVESTED IN BOEING 767, 777 AIRCRAFT TO EXTEND THEIR LIFE -CONF CALL.UNITED AIRLINES CEO MUNOZ SAYS ULTIMATE GOAL OF REGULATORS GLOBALLY IS TO SCRUTINIZE 737 MAX AND 'MAKE THE RIGHT DECISIONS' FOR SAFETY.UNITED AIRLINES CEO MUNOZ SAYS POTENTIAL STAGGERED RETURN OF 737 MAX WOULD NOT LIKELY IMPACT PLANS: 'WE'LL CROSS THAT BRIDGE WHEN WE COME TO THAT'.UNITED AIRLINES CEO MUNOZ SAYS EMPLOYEES DESERVE TO HAVE COMPENSATION INCREASES AS PROFITS GROW OVER TIME.UNITED AIRLINES CEO MUNOZ SAYS HAS ABILITY TO KEEP COSTS FLAT BY 'CONSTANTLY GETTING MORE EFFICIENT'."}
{'symbol': 'UNH', 'date': '2019-10-16 08:30:00', 'title': 'UnitedHealth Group Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'UNITEDHEALTH GROUP REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $14.90 TO $15.00.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $14.15 TO $14.25.QTRLY NET EARNINGS PER SHARE WERE $3.67, ADJUSTED NET EARNINGS PER SHARE WERE $3.88.QTRLY TOTAL REVENUES OF $60.4 BILLION GREW BY 7% OR $3.8 BILLION YEAR-OVER-YEAR.QTRLY ADJUSTED NET EARNINGS PER SHARE WERE $3.88.140 BASIS POINT YEAR-OVER-YEAR INCREASE IN MEDICAL CARE RATIO TO 82.4 PERCENT IN QUARTER.Q3 MEDICAL COST TRENDS REMAINED IN LINE WITH EXPECTATIONS.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $14.83 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.OPTUM Q3 2019 REVENUES GREW BY 13.3 PERCENT OR $3.4 BILLION YEAR-OVER-YEAR TO $28.8 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $3.75, REVENUE VIEW $59.79 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
